1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,900
Shawn is terrified of heights!

3
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:28,860
You've gone way too far!

4
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:30,780
That's a personal insult!

5
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:33,660
Shawn!

6
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:39,420
I'm sorry, Shawn. I was wrong.

7
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:42,300
Wow. You've got some nerve pulling a stunt like that.

8
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,700
Should we put on a

9
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,140
fancy Yo-Yo performance?

10
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,200
Yeah!

11
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,430
The joint Jianghai and Chengnan Team

12
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,900
Yo-Yo Bonfire Party

13
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:53,340
is Officially starting now!

14
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Episode 24

15
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,820
Get down from there!

16
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:06,750
I said, get down!

17
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,220
Come down! Now!

18
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:38,940
Quiet, everyone. Settle down.

19
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,380
Next up is the talent show.

20
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:44,700
First, let's welcome Coach Sarah from the Chengnan Team
to perform for us! Give her a big round of applause!

21
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,460
Quiet down, everyone.

22
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,350
Your Coach Tony

23
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,300
loved to sing back when he was in Sports Academy.

24
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:57,630
He used to sing "The Grapes of Turpan" beautifully.

25
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:59,580
Let's have Coach Tony give us a song!

26
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:06,780
Coach Tony! Give us a song!

27
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:11,100
Nah, I'd better not. I won't sing.

28
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,060
My voice is gone.

29
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,460
No way! You have to give us one!

30
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:23,100
Alright, just a short bit.

31
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:34,140
"When Klim joined the army,
he was sent to the frontier outpost..."

32
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:40,860
"Before he left, he planted a single grapevine..."

33
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,260
My voice is pretty rough.

34
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:46,140
We should get someone who can actually sing up here.

35
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,060
I'll do it! I'll go!

36
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,460
You can't sing?

37
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:51,900
Yeah!

38
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:55,740
Watch. This is what they mean by
"a True Master never reveals himself." Got it?

39
00:04:56,680 --> 00:05:01,500
"White clouds drift across the vast blue sky..."

40
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,100
Are you starting to feel like you don't wanna go back?

41
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:24,060
I never imagined there'd be so many Yo-Yo Players here,

42
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,940
and that they'd all be this skilled.

43
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
T-then you...

44
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:36,510
And now, we've reached

45
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,980
the highlight of our Evening!

46
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,900
Fireworks!

47
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,260
Oh, awesome!

48
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:57,180
Wow, it's so beautiful!

49
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:01,980
Yeah. It's almost like a Seven-Colored Light.

50
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:13,500
So... are you still going back to America?

51
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:17,820
Yeah.

52
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,580
But I'll come back and visit a lot.

53
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:54,300
Don't worry, I'm coming!

54
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,040
You full now?

55
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,350
And what about you? Last time it rained,

56
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,780
couldn't you have soaked up a
few more nutrients on your own?

57
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,550
You're a big plant now.

58
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,500
Well then, I'll just give you some extra food.

59
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,260
Looks like it's time for a trim.

60
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,780
Mickey, hurry it up!

61
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,700
It's bad to be late for Training.

62
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:58,620
When am I ever gonna get to sleep in on a weekend?

63
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,740
Just go to practice.

64
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,580
Maybe we should just skip it.

65
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:39,420
Better just go to practice.

66
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:48,540
Mom, I'm heading to School for Training!

67
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,940
Teddy, you're Training even on the weekend?

68
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,860
Did you look over those Chemistry
tutoring materials I gave you?

69
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,740
Yeah, I looked at them.

70
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,500
"Yeah, I looked at them."

71
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,110
You need to really put your heart into it.

72
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:00,060
I know, Mom. I'm going now.

73
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:11,580
Mickey, don't use an excuse like that

74
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:14,460
to go buy a new Yo-Yo holster

75
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:16,380
instead of going to Practice.

76
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,780
Leo's never gonna agree to that.

77
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:21,630
Sis, if you just talk to Leo,

78
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,100
of course he'll agree!

79
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:26,460
But the reason you wanna skip is just... so trivial.

80
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,860
I just can't come up with a good excuse.

81
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:29,820
What?

82
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,710
Sis, you don't get it.

83
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:34,620
This Yo-Yo holster is super important to me.

84
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,020
It inspires me and fires me up!

85
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:39,420
When I'm wearing it, I'm just... really in the zone.

86
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,340
Doesn't Shawn always say

87
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:45,250
"that feelings are super important for a Top-level Player."

88
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,540
Alright, fine, Sis. I'm off!

89
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,900
I'm not gonna cover for you.

90
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:56,220
Why can't you just go another day? It's the exact same thing.

91
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:00,540
Are you going to Practice, or not?

92
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,300
You decide my fate.

93
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:07,820
This side's for Practice.

94
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,880
Or Play.

95
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,420
Practice.

96
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:18,780
Practice.

97
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,140
Practice again.

98
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:23,580
Alright, one last time.

99
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:26,460
Matthew!

100
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:29,340
Play!

101
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:30,780
Let's go.

102
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:49,020
Where's Mickey?

103
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:53,820
Mickey? Uh, he had something going on today.

104
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,330
So many people are sick today.

105
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,430
Monica is sick.

106
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,870
And Matthew's Mom is sick.

107
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:04,950
Teddy's Grandpa is sick.

108
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:08,700
Couldn't Teddy just come up with a different excuse for once?

109
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,140
Last weekend it was his Grandpa.

110
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:11,580
This weekend it's his Grandpa again.

111
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,430
And last weekend, wasn't his Grandpa sick because

112
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,940
he lost his dentures?

113
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,220
You know, the absolute worst liar

114
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,590
has gotta be Chuck.

115
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,540
He actually said he's working out to get in shape

116
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,460
for the upcoming Tournament.

117
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:29,790
He actually had the nerve to use
that as an excuse to fool people.

118
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,260
And Mini, you're one to talk.

119
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:32,670
Mickey's excuse didn't make any sense at all.

120
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:34,140
How could you have agreed to that?

121
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:37,020
I know, I know.

122
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,900
But I just couldn't win the argument with him.

123
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:41,820
And if I'd said no,

124
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:45,180
he would've just followed me around like a robot

125
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:47,580
whose batteries had been yanked out.

126
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:51,420
Lately, everyone's been acting like
a bunch of lifeless puppets.

127
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,910
They've totally lost their fighting spirit.

128
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:54,300
I agree

129
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:55,740
Ever since we got back from the Falcon Camp,

130
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,180
everyone's attitude has completely changed.

131
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:58,590
They think that just because we beat the Chengnan Team,

132
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,060
Victory is already in the bag.

133
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,940
So what are we supposed to do about it?

134
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,820
Well, we can't be soft like you.

135
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,660
That was beautiful! We're winning!

136
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:25,500
I still have a turn left.

137
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,380
No, don't!

138
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,540
Come on, move.

139
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,460
You should bring out your rook.

140
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
No No,

141
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,660
Just move your knight.

142
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:47,580
Move the rook. Bring out the rook.

143
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,500
Capture with the rook.

144
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:53,340
Ugh, I told you to move the knight
and you just wouldn't listen.

145
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,140
Looks like you should just move your own knight.

146
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,900
Hurry, grab a couple more outfits for me to look at.

147
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:29,340
What do you think of this one?

148
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,060
Well? What do you think? Do you like it?

149
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,460
I think...

150
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:40,860
Come on, say something! Give me your opinion!

151
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:43,740
We all think it looks really bad.

152
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,980
I actually had a stomach ache at first,

153
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:52,860
but then my friend from the Club called and told me

154
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,260
my idol was gonna be at the airport today.

155
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,100
So I went to go buy him a gift.

156
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,980
I looked and looked, but I just
couldn't decide what to get him.

157
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,870
And before I knew it,

158
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,820
I'd found an outfit I liked for myself.

159
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,260
I went to visit my Grandpa,

160
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,440
but he was already feeling a lot better
and had gone for a walk in the park.

161
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,540
So I went to the park to find him,

162
00:15:13,180 --> 00:15:14,940
but after looking everywhere, I couldn't track him down.

163
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,340
I searched and searched, but no luck.

164
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:20,700
So I just ended up watching some
old guys play chess in the park.

165
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:27,230
I'm not lying! I really was working out to lose weight.

166
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:31,260
I need to be in good shape for the Tournament.

167
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:34,590
So I was riding my Bike and playing video games,

168
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,540
specifically picking activities that burn the most energy.

169
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:39,900
My Mom's not sick.

170
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,260
But Chuck said I could use that
as an excuse to skip Practice.

171
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,100
I'm just really worried I'm
not gonna grow tall enough, so...

172
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,460
So I decided to go home and sleep more.

173
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:53,820
Mickey, what are you even talking about?

174
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,220
Sis, I'm serious.

175
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,620
Yesterday, I read in a book

176
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,500
that sleeping more can make you taller. So I...

177
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,420
So that's what I did.

178
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,820
You guys could've saved yourselves the trouble
of coming up with all these excuses.

179
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,000
What?

180
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:09,630
Do you all think you're so amazing that
you don't need to Practice anymore?

181
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,100
Is that it?

182
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:13,600
Lately, the Coach has been swamped with School Business,

183
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,500
He's too busy,

184
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,340
so Training is entirely up to us now.

185
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,230
Every single one of us matters.

186
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,220
We all have a huge responsibility.

187
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:23,580
Because in a Team Competition, the Final Score
is the sum of everyone's Individual Scores.

188
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:25,500
If any one Player loses a significant amount of points,

189
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:27,420
it affects the entire Team's Results.

190
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,780
All our past Training and hard work would be for nothing.

191
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,540
We can't just beat the Chengnan Team once

192
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,210
and then let ourselves get this complacent.

193
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,820
If we slow down now, other teams are gonna catch up.

194
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:43,210
Captain, don't worry.

195
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,500
Even if they were riding a rocket ship.

196
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:49,510
They wouldn't be able to come close to us.

197
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:52,350
Yeah! Last time we beat the Chengnan Team,

198
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:53,630
the Jianghai Team's reputation skyrocketed.

199
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:57,180
I doubt there's anyone left who can take us down!

200
00:16:57,640 --> 00:17:00,660
That's nonsense! That last win was just by a hair.

201
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:04,380
I've heard that the Chengnan Team is stepping up their Training.

202
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:05,820
We cannot underestimate them.

203
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,220
So from now on, our raining

204
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:09,660
can only increase, never decrease.

205
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,230
Does everyone understand?

206
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,420
We understand.

207
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:19,740
Captain, I propose we reform the way we Practice.

208
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,180
Reform it how?

209
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:23,100
Well, practice takes persistence.

210
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,950
But having everyone travel all the way
to the Training Hall every weekend

211
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,940
is such a hassle.

212
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,380
We could all just

213
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:29,870
practice at home instead.

214
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,040
That's right.

215
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,700
Yeah! And the AC in the Training Room
is never cold enough anyway.

216
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,140
It's not as nice as practicing at home.

217
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,730
The biggest issue is that we're wasting
so much time just travelling.

218
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:41,820
You know, you've just wasted all that
time with this pointless chatter.

219
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,710
Everyone, just stop complaining.

220
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:46,110
If the Jianghai Team still wants to win the Championship,

221
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:48,540
then our weekend Training Sessions are non-negotiable.

222
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:49,980
Yes, exactly.

223
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,900
Not only should we keep the Weekend Training,

224
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:54,710
we should also keep up with the theory lessons.

225
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,000
So dizzy.

226
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,550
You see, when you start to feel dizzy,

227
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:01,500
that means you've entered a state of primordial chaos.

228
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:03,390
It's just like the darkness right before dawn.

229
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,860
The light is almost about to break through.

230
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:08,220
Captain, I formally request that we

231
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:10,000
add one more Yo-Yo theory class every week.

232
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,580
I want to share all my insights with everyone.

233
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,000
I truly believe

234
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,380
this will make our Jianghai Team stronger.

235
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
A true kindred spirit is so hard to find.

236
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:23,900
Come over to my place tonight. Let's talk.

237
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:27,900
Good thing we ducked out fast.

238
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,340
Otherwise, with one word from Leo,

239
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:32,190
and him agreeing to Shawn's idea,

240
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,660
we'd be totally doomed.

241
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:36,060
Exactly, The hardest thing to endure in life

242
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,980
is having to listen to Shawn's lecture.

243
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,420
Every time I do, every cell in my body

244
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:40,860
just wants to stop breathing,

245
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:42,780
just to escape the agony.

246
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,220
Ugh, hey, Matthew.

247
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:45,660
How come lately

248
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,060
you're starting to sound more and more like Popcorn?

249
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:49,020
Who, me?

250
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:50,940
It's Zoe!

251
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,860
Oh no, quick, hide!

252
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,520
Why are you hiding?

253
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,060
Perfect chance to ask her

254
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:01,500
about the Chengnan Team.

255
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:02,460
What's there to even ask?

256
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:03,870
You don't seriously think

257
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:04,860
the Chengnan Team could actually surpass us?

258
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:06,500
True...

259
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:10,620
But "know yourself and know your enemy"
is always the best military strategy.

260
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:11,700
I believe

261
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:14,460
As long as you, Matthew,
are willing to open your mouth and ask,

262
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,270
info about the Chengnan Team will just
come flooding in on its own.

263
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:20,700
If you wanna know so bad, you go ask!

264
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,100
Zoe's coming! Ah!

265
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:25,020
Where? Where?

266
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:27,420
What's your problem?

267
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:29,820
Look at you, you're terrified.

268
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,260
Stop joking around like that.

269
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:32,500
It's not funny.

270
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,100
Matthew!

271
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Matthew!

272
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,110
I just saw you plain as day.

273
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:47,100
And you actually tried to hide from me?

274
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,460
There's just no escaping fate.

275
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,820
So, uh... did you need something?

276
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:55,740
Do I need a reason to talk to you?

277
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,180
I just wanted to chat.

278
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:59,120
C-Chat? About what?

279
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:00,200
Anything!

280
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:05,340
So, how's Practice been going lately?

281
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:07,740
Uh... it's... it's going alright.

282
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:09,880
You still haven't perfected your Shockwave move, have you?

283
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,510
Oh, come on. What's there to even ask about that?

284
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:13,980
Oh, so it's a Secret now?

285
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,820
Hey, Zoe.

286
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:20,220
How many times a week does your Chengnan Team practice?

287
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,620
Hmph. I'm keeping that a Secret, too.

288
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:25,500
You're keeping that a secret, too? Come on, be real.

289
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:26,940
How often you guys train

290
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:29,340
doesn't really matter to us anyway.

291
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:30,780
You're already yesterday's news.

292
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,180
We don't even think about you guys.

293
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,100
What did you just say, Teddy?

294
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:37,020
Whoa, no need to shout.

295
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,460
So unladylike.

296
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,860
What did you say? Say that again.

297
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:43,740
Whoa, scary! Hey, Matthew!

298
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,180
What's Matthew got to do with this?

299
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,630
Teddy, if you don't repeat what you
just said right now, you're not a man.

300
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,170
Alright, alright, stop fighting.

301
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,820
A real Mmn lets his actions speak, not his words.

302
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:57,180
Oh, so you want a match, is that it? Fine, let's do it.

303
00:20:58,120 --> 00:21:01,020
Forget it. A true gentleman doesn't fight with a lady.

304
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:04,860
Hmph. Too bad I don't see any "true gentleman"
standing in front of me.

305
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:07,890
Zoe, I was only cutting you some slack

306
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,760
because you're a girl.

307
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,100
But since you're pushing me,

308
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,540
you asked for it.

309
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:14,950
I don't need you to cut me any slack.

310
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:18,750
Fine, have it your way.

311
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:20,220
I'll show you what the Jianghai Team is made of!

312
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:23,580
Hmph. The Chengnan Team doesn't scare that easily.

